\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Frontier analysis: capability cannot fix coordination overhead. (a) Total cost scaling with perfect agents (capability $= 1.0$); dotted lines show theoretical minimum (frontier) governance. (b) Fully Connected governance fraction \emph  {increases} as agent capability improves---because implementation cost shrinks while governance remains constant. (c) Cost efficiency (effective output per token) with Study~3 empirical data overlaid (gold stars), confirming monotonic degradation.}}{15}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frontier}{{5}{15}{Frontier analysis: capability cannot fix coordination overhead. (a) Total cost scaling with perfect agents (capability $= 1.0$); dotted lines show theoretical minimum (frontier) governance. (b) Fully Connected governance fraction \emph {increases} as agent capability improves---because implementation cost shrinks while governance remains constant. (c) Cost efficiency (effective output per token) with Study~3 empirical data overlaid (gold stars), confirming monotonic degradation}{figure.5}{}}
